        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_dc973ce71a5046bdb75c4f22715b88b9",
      "statement": "When a potential coverage defense is identified, the claims manual requires an approved reservation of rights within 10 days, with specific known facts and issues, and investigation continues after the reservation unless directed otherwise.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://manuals/claims/manual.md#L481-L503",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:af38f782a8f1d772e5b78f3f623c4fc44de1bd8f5daa0ebcf19c0d2d20f706bd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_27a38dedf63d4cb0b6811be0b704ab37",
      "statement": "Roof causation analysis must distinguish source, water or damage path, timing and duration, direct event damage, and pre-existing wear, deterioration, maintenance, workmanship, or betterment; the adjuster must inspect relevant roof and interior areas and compare damaged and undamaged conditions before estimating.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://guidelines/claims/roof-claim-handling.md#L487-L501",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a0dc7dc5a2742bff3531d60bcd01f7d71426423a40345571b3b36eba4c88036d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://manuals/claims/manual.md#L75-L97",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:44a774c7a7a8ac83343355686fe532fe61e31f464fff2d231e0523a467146b41:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9d7f6f5f240942719b72050b2e83d310",
      "statement": "Under HO-3 2024-03, wind and hail are covered perils subject to policy exclusions, interior rain or similar precipitation damage requires direct wind or hail damage to first create an opening, cosmetic roof-surfacing damage is excluded, and wind or hail damage impairing the roof's ability to shed water is covered; the roof-schedule trigger age alone does not establish coverage.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://forms/HO/MS/HO-3/2024-03.md#L631-L639",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9ba27503ca340c9cb997b7c6483936735315125888e3e42fccbed63ff7b563b8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8122b11a247d43d1acb700017b281825",
      "statement": "Roof age is evidence for claim investigation and valuation, not an independent claim denial rule: age must be tied to the damaged roof surfacing and supported by reliable records or other evidence, while Florida OIR-2023-04 requires an independent claim evaluation under the policy and facts.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://bulletins/FL/oir-2023-04-roof-age-nonrenewal.md#L239-L255",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:aeca85749a7358c9e627fc2c447ef000534a2901e93c6c1a3050ac45ef2fa963:"
        },
        {
